{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486987649,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDcxOTkwMDI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1284","origin":"github"},"title":"GitRepo.publish() needs more flexible API","message":"At present I can specify exactly one refspec to be pushed. However `publish()` needs more flexible ways. Push multiple branches at once, honor `remote.\u003cname\u003e.push` configuration(s), and, in addition, push a particular set of tags branches.\n\nFrom my PoV, a low-level approach would be to be able to flexibly pass Git configuration items to the `GitRepo` method. Ala `git -c var=value -c .... push`. This way `publish()` could easily, and dynamically amend an existing configuration. More convenient would be a way to list any number of values for `remote.\u003cname\u003e.push` directly, instead of, or amending the current `refspec` argument.\n\nA resolution of this issue is required for moving forward with things like #1275, and selective publication in general, without having to introduce custom code wrapping each `push()` call.","files":null}]}